---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout title="Dan McSpirit">
  <div id="shell">
    <!-- IDENTITY COLUMN -->
    <aside class="col col-identity">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div class="name">Dan McSpirit</div>
        <div class="metadata">Denver, Colorado</div>
      </div>

      <h1 style="margin-bottom: 26px;">
        Closing the gap. <br class="mbreak" />
        Creating value.
      </h1>

      <!-- Portrait Card -->
      <div style="position: relative; margin-bottom: 30px; margin-top: 60px;">
        <!-- Portrait Image -->
        <img
          src="/portrait-sketch.png"
          alt="Dan McSpirit"
          style="position: absolute; top: -60px; right: 0; width: 58%; height: auto; max-width: 280px; display: block;"
        />

        <!-- Card -->
        <div style="display: flex; height: 260px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--paper-dark);">
          <div
            style="position: relative; flex: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: flex-end; padding: 24px 18px 24px 22px;"
          >
            <div style="font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.16; color: #23426A; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
              <div>Investor</div>
              <div>Builder</div>
              <div>Teacher</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            style="position: relative; flex: 0 0 58%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--paper-dark) 0%, rgba(237, 231, 217, 0) 27%);"
          >
            <div
              style="position: absolute; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 72px; background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(237, 231, 217, 0) 0%, var(--paper-dark) 100%);"
            ></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Body Prose -->
      <p style="margin-bottom: 28px;">
        How capital is allocated determines whether value gets created or destroyed. I work as an investor and builder of analytical tools to direct capital toward its highest returning use. I bring that same discipline to substitute teaching to help students close the gap between where they are and where they could be.
      </p>

      <div class="divider"></div>

      <!-- Hard-won Truth -->
      <div class="section-label muted" style="margin-bottom: 14px;">Hard-won truth</div>
      <blockquote style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
        "Finance golden rule: You can't get somethin' for nothin'."
      </blockquote>
      <p class="body-sm" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        Risk and return are inextricably linked; if you can't see the risk, you haven't looked hard enough.
      </p>

      <div style="height: 1px; background: var(--rule); margin: 0 0 24px;"></div>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <div class="section-label muted" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">Contact</div>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 14px;" class="body-sm">
        Open to independent valuation work, diligence on specific names, and building or reviewing models, including AI-built ones.
      </p>
      <a href="mailto:mcspiritdaniel@gmail.com" class="lnk" style="display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        mcspiritdaniel@gmail.com
      </a>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 24px;" class="body-sm">
        Analysis on this site is for informational purposes only and is not investment advice. I may hold positions in the companies and assets discussed.
      </p>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; align-items: center; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.04em;">
        <a href="https://x.com/danmcspirit" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">
          X ↗
        </a>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/danmcspirit" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">
          LinkedIn ↗
        </a>
        <span style="color: var(--faint);">© 2026</span>
      </div>

      <div style="height: 46px;"></div>
      <div class="scrollfade"></div>
    </aside>

    <!-- WORK COLUMN -->
    <section class="col col-work">
      <div class="stickyhead">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; margin-bottom: 10px;">
          <span class="col-header-label">Experience</span>
          <span class="scrollcue">scroll ↓</span>
        </div>
        <p class="subtitle">
          The thread through every role: a pull toward steep learning curves and a habit of leading the climb.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pad">
        <!-- Advisory & Investing Section -->
        <div class="section-label" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Advisory & Investing</div>

        <!-- Otherwhere Capital Entry -->
        <div style="padding-bottom: 24px; margin-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #E2DACA;">
          <div class="work-date" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">2019 — Present</div>
          <h2 class="work-title" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">Otherwhere Capital</h2>
          <div class="work-role" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Principal | Independent Research & Investing</div>
          <div class="body-sm">
            Fundamental research and investing in public equities, using AI as a research associate and a verification process to catch what it gets wrong. I have partnered with founders on capitalization strategy, financial modeling and valuation work, and co-founded a manufacturing operation.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Capital Markets Section -->
        <div class="section-label muted" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Capital Markets</div>

        <!-- BMO Capital Markets Entry -->
        <div style="padding-bottom: 24px; margin-bottom: 22px; border-bottom: 1px solid #E2DACA;">
          <div class="work-date muted" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">2004 — 2019</div>
          <h2 class="work-title" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">BMO Capital Markets</h2>
          <div class="work-role" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Director | Institutional Equity Research</div>
          <div class="body-sm">
            Provided institutional-grade valuation and investment analysis for a portfolio of publicly traded companies, advising global asset managers on capital allocation.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- First Albany Entry -->
        <div style="padding-bottom: 24px; margin-bottom: 30px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);">
          <div class="work-date muted" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">1996 — 2004</div>
          <h2 class="work-title" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">First Albany Corporation</h2>
          <div class="work-role" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Senior Associate, Investment Banking | Analyst, CFO Office</div>
          <div class="body-sm">Executed middle-market transactions, including debt and equity capital raises and M&A&D mandates, and supported firm-wide financial strategy.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- In the Classroom Section -->
        <div class="section-label" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">In the Classroom</div>

        <div style="background: var(--paper-dark); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 3px; padding: 20px; margin-bottom: 34px;">
          <h3 class="work-title" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Denver Public Schools</h3>
          <p class="body-sm">
            Currently a Guest Teacher in the DPS system. Teaching pulls on the same instinct as the work: take something complex, find the first principle, and make it usable. The most honest test of whether you understand an idea is whether you can hand it to someone else.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--paper-dark); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 3px; padding: 20px; margin-bottom: 34px;">
          <h3 class="work-title" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">subin</h3>
          <p class="body-sm" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
            Substitute teaching gives you no established authority and limited time to find your footing. I created subin to replace that scramble with a ready-made game plan for the day and additional resources to help when the plan doesn't hold, all built directly from my own personal experiences in the classroom.
          </p>
          <a href="https://joinsubin.org" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">
            view ↗
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Education Section -->
        <div class="section-label" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Education & Credentials</div>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 11px; margin-bottom: 30px;">
          <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px;">
            <span style="color: var(--navy); flex-shrink: 0;">•</span>
            <div class="body-sm">The Wharton School, Advanced Finance Program (WMP21)</div>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px;">
            <span style="color: var(--navy); flex-shrink: 0;">•</span>
            <div class="body-sm">CFA Charter</div>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px;">
            <span style="color: var(--navy); flex-shrink: 0;">•</span>
            <div class="body-sm">CMA Certificate</div>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px;">
            <span style="color: var(--navy); flex-shrink: 0;">•</span>
            <div class="body-sm">FSA Credential</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Community Involvement Section -->
        <div class="section-label" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Community Involvement</div>

        <div style="padding-bottom: 24px; margin-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #E2DACA;">
          <div class="work-date muted" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">2025 — Present</div>
          <h2 class="work-title" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">ICMA Exam Review Committee Member</h2>
          <div class="work-role" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">IMA | Institute of Management Accountants</div>
          <div class="body-sm">Help shape the rigor and relevance of the Certified Management Accountant (CMA) certification by reviewing and developing exam content.</div>
        </div>

        <div style="padding-bottom: 24px; margin-bottom: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #E2DACA;">
          <div class="work-date muted" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">2021 — 2023</div>
          <h2 class="work-title" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">Foundation Board Member & Investment Program Advisor</h2>
          <div class="work-role" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Upcycled Food Association</div>
          <div class="body-sm">Guided financial strategy and provided board governance for a mission-driven organization dedicated to sustainable food systems.</div>
        </div>

        <div style="padding-bottom: 24px; margin-bottom: 46px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);">
          <div class="work-date muted" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">2021 — 2022</div>
          <h2 class="work-title" style="margin-bottom: 4px;">FSA Level II Subject Matter Expert</h2>
          <div class="work-role" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">IFRS Foundation</div>
          <div class="body-sm">Developed sustainability exam content ensuring technical rigor and real-world practitioner relevance.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="scrollfade"></div>
    </section>

    <!-- PROJECTS COLUMN -->
    <section class="col col-projects">
      <div class="stickyhead">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; margin-bottom: 10px;">
          <span class="col-header-label" style="color: var(--ink);">Featured Projects</span>
          <span class="scrollcue">scroll ↓</span>
        </div>
        <p class="subtitle">
          Institutional-grade analysis and insights, deepened and expressed through AI-powered tools.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pad">
        <!-- Featured Projects with Collapsed Groups -->
        <div class="projects-groups">
          <!-- Group 1: Process & Verification -->
          <div class="project-group">
            <div class="group-header expanded" onclick="this.classList.toggle('expanded')">
              <div class="group-toggle">−</div>
              <div class="group-info">
                <div class="group-title">Process & Verification</div>
                <div class="group-subtitle">How I think about building reliable models</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="group-content">
              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="/sbet-build-process.pdf" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">What It Actually Takes to Trust AI-Built Analysis</h2>
                  </a>
                  <a href="/sbet-build-process.pdf" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">view ↗</a>
                </div>
                <p class="pcard-body" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                  An account of building an institutional-grade valuation model with AI, and of the eight times it was wrong. Not one was an arithmetic error. Every one was a claim about the output — a stale figure from an earlier build, a crossed reference, a share basis that didn't match the line beside it. What caught them was a regression harness, a second AI system with no stake in the first one's conclusions, and review. The work didn't shrink; it moved from construction to verification.
                </p>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                  <span class="tag">claude chat + design</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="/value-framework.pdf" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">Value Creation Framework</h2>
                  </a>
                  <a href="/value-framework.pdf" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">view ↗</a>
                </div>
                <p class="pcard-body" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                  The principles that guide my work as an investor and builder. How capital allocation determines whether value gets created or destroyed. Price vs value, leverage, risk, verification, and why the discipline of the work matters more than getting lucky.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Group 2: Deep Analysis -->
          <div class="project-group">
            <div class="group-header" onclick="this.classList.toggle('expanded')">
              <div class="group-toggle">+</div>
              <div class="group-info">
                <div class="group-title">Deep Analysis</div>
                <div class="group-subtitle">The work behind the headlines</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="group-content">
              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="/iren-power-pricing-funding.pdf" target="_blank" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">IREN: Power, Pricing and Funding</h2>
                  </a>
                  <a href="/iren-power-pricing-funding.pdf" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">view ↗</a>
                </div>
                <p class="pcard-body" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                  An independent valuation of IREN testing whether scarce powered capacity in Texas helps or hurts the company. At ~$42 a share in October 2026, the price assumes today's pricing, utilization and financing persist, and the bigger risks are contract pricing, GPU lives and funding a ~$55bn build rather than the Texas queue.
                </p>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                  <span class="tag">ms excel</span>
                  <span class="tag">claude chat</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="/eth-valuation-analysis-agentic-finance.pdf" target="_blank" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">ETH Valuation Analysis: Agentic Finance</h2>
                  </a>
                  <a href="/eth-valuation-analysis-agentic-finance.pdf" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">view ↗</a>
                </div>
                <p class="pcard-body" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                  A two-slide analysis of what ETH's price actually rests on. Fees support roughly 9% of today's price. Read through a security-budget rule, the price instead needs Ethereum to secure ~$2.3T of stablecoins and tokenized assets by 2035. A second lens converts a ~$4T agentic revenue estimate into the balances behind it, and finds today's price needs only ~0.5% of them on Ethereum, if the assets follow the revenue.
                </p>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                  <span class="tag">ms excel</span>
                  <span class="tag">claude code</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="/sbet-discount-return-analysis.pdf" target="_blank" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">SBET Discount & Return Analysis</h2>
                  </a>
                  <a href="/sbet-discount-return-analysis.pdf" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">view ↗</a>
                </div>
                <p class="pcard-body" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                  Sharplink holds almost nothing but ETH, yet its stock has traded below the value of those net assets on every session for a year. Rebuilt from primary filings, the analysis shows the discount's swings fade within weeks, but only back to about 0.8× NAV, while ETH drives about three-quarters of the stock's moves. With the market not closing the gap, the question shifts to management and what it can do to grow ETH per share.
                </p>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                  <span class="tag">ms excel</span>
                  <span class="tag">claude code</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="/linea-return-decomposition.pdf" target="_blank" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">LINEA Return Decomposition</h2>
                  </a>
                  <a href="/linea-return-decomposition.pdf" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">view ↗</a>
                </div>
                <p class="pcard-body" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                  A daily log-return decomposition of the LINEA token, splitting every price move into four terms that add exactly: ETH, network fees, the valuation multiple, and circulating supply. Built from primary on-chain data — 252,887 transfer events replayed from the genesis mint, supply reconciled to the token contract to the wei, and network fees computed block by block — with no explorer labels or aggregator figures. The result: since the dual burn went live, 38 million tokens burned against 16 billion unlocked, and a market paying 176× fees for adoption that has not yet arrived.
                </p>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                  <span class="tag">ms excel</span>
                  <span class="tag">claude code</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="/sbet-return-contribution.pdf" target="_blank" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">SBET Return Contribution</h2>
                  </a>
                  <a href="/sbet-return-contribution.pdf" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">view ↗</a>
                </div>
                <p class="pcard-body" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                  Sharplink holds ETH, but owning the stock is not the same as owning the asset. Decomposing thirteen months of returns separates what came from ETH, what came from the multiple the market puts on net asset value, and what leaked away in dilution. The mix depends on how long you hold — the multiple drove half of a single day's move and a third of the period, because it mean-reverts and ETH doesn't.
                </p>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                  <span class="tag">ms excel</span>
                  <span class="tag">claude code</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="/iren-valuation-analysis.pdf" target="_blank" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">IREN Valuation Analysis</h2>
                  </a>
                  <a href="/iren-valuation-analysis.pdf" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">view ↗</a>
                </div>
                <p class="pcard-body" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                  IREN is two investments stacked: a data centre building, and a decision to fill it with hardware rather than lease it out. With a third of its capital in real estate and more than 80% of announced capacity still to be built, the market is paying for contract pricing less than where the company signs today.
                </p>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                  <span class="tag">ms excel</span>
                  <span class="tag">claude chat + design</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Group 3: Interactive Applications -->
          <div class="project-group">
            <div class="group-header" onclick="this.classList.toggle('expanded')">
              <div class="group-toggle">+</div>
              <div class="group-info">
                <div class="group-title">Interactive Applications</div>
                <div class="group-subtitle">Analysis built to engage and explore</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="group-content">
              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="https://sbet-absolute-valuation.vercel.app/" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">SBET Absolute Valuation</h2>
                  </a>
                  <a href="https://sbet-absolute-valuation.vercel.app/" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">view ↗</a>
                </div>
                <p class="pcard-body" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                  Digital asset treasury companies get valued on ETH per share, a metric that rises on any buyback at any price and never registers a dollar of operating expense. This model puts NAV per share beside it and prices the warrant stack properly — treasury stock method where warrants are in the money, a Black-Scholes deduction where they are not. The anchor is what SBET is worth if management never touches the capital markets again; everything above that line is what you are paying for the machine.
                </p>
                <p style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--faint); margin-bottom: 12px;">Best viewed on desktop</p>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                  <span class="tag">ms excel</span>
                  <span class="tag">claude chat + design + code</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="https://eth-valuation-analysis.vercel.app/" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">ETH Valuation Analysis</h2>
                  </a>
                  <a href="https://eth-valuation-analysis.vercel.app/" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">view ↗</a>
                </div>
                <p class="pcard-body" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                  A sum-of-the-parts DCF that values ETH as programmable infrastructure, modeling composability, restaking, and agentic settlement as calibrated overlap rather than a comp-multiple guess. Built as a single dial-able valuation with no bull/base/bear scenarios. Simply adjust any assumption and watch one number, value per ETH, update live.
                </p>
                <p style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--faint); margin-bottom: 12px;">Best viewed on desktop</p>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                  <span class="tag">ms excel</span>
                  <span class="tag">claude chat + design + code</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="https://spcx-valuation-analysis.vercel.app/" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">SpaceX (SPCX) Valuation Analysis</h2>
                  </a>
                  <a href="https://spcx-valuation-analysis.vercel.app/" target="_blank" class="lnk" style="font-size: 11px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 0; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;">view ↗</a>
                </div>
                <p class="pcard-body" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
                  SpaceX defies a single valuation line. This sum-of-the-parts framework breaks the business into its constituent segments and lets you stress-test the assumptions that drive the range. Rebuilt from Excel into an interactive app you can actually challenge.
                </p>
                <p style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--faint); margin-bottom: 12px;">Best viewed on desktop</p>
                <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                  <span class="tag">ms excel</span>
                  <span class="tag">claude chat + design + code</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="project-item">
                <div class="project-title-row">
                  <a href="https://linea-valuation-analysis.vercel.app/" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
                    <h2 class="project-title">LINEA Valuation Analysis</h2>
